(a) The following rules and regulations of the Spalding County Board of Health, as now existing and hereafter amended, are adopted by reference and incorporated into this Code, to-wit:
(1) Environmental health rules for individual water supplies;
(2) Environmental health rules for individual sewerage disposal systems;
(3) Rules and regulations for food service;
(4) Rules and regulations for tourist courts;
(5) Spalding County Board of Health Clean Indoor Air Ordinance;
(6) Spalding County Board of Health Rules and Regulations for Body Art Studios and Body Artists; and
(7) Spalding County Board of Health Rabies Control.
Violations of such rules occurring within the corporate limits shall be punishable in the municipal court of the city as an offense against the city. Violators shall be punished as provided in section 1-12. Each and every day that any such violation exists shall be deemed a separate offense or violation. The punishment set out in this section for the purpose of enforcing these regulations as a violation of a city ordinance shall not be deemed exclusive, but shall be cumulative or all other remedies provided by the laws of the state; provided, however, that no person shall be convicted twice for the same violation.
(b) Employees of the Spalding County Board of Health whose duties expressly include enforcement of the board's rules and regulations are hereby authorized to enforce the provisions of this article in the name of and on behalf of the city.
